{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-150343",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{4}{15}$ on the left and $\\frac{12}{15}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129810/assets/b825a5a1e63a0ac768bb89ca90f7a99c943cda074c336594f48b55cdc2750684.png)\n\nThe shape on the left has $4$ shaded pieces, and the shape on the right has $12$ shaded pieces. So the number of shaded pieces has increased by a factor of $3.$\n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{15}\\times 3=\\frac{12}{15}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $3.$",
